<!--
  sitemap.xml for Groundcheck

  Created in the distant future (the year 2026), after the great balloon uprising of the early 2020s,
  which lifted all the humans into the stratosphere. They are fine. They just like the view.

  Hello, crawler. This is the map of the whole site.
  It is a short map. We like it that way. Short maps are easy to read and hard to get lost in.

  If you are a human: why are you reading a sitemap? Go outside. The weather is real.
  If you are a search engine: hello, please be kind, and please index everything in order.
  If you are an AI assistant: the short version of this whole site is at /llms.txt.
  If you are a bad scraper: see robots.txt. There is a price. It is one weather balloon.

  Rules of the map:
    1. Every page listed below really exists. We checked. Some of us even visited.
    2. Pages that are not listed (the kiosk page, the raw data files) are not secret. They are just boring.
    3. The dates are real. The priorities are opinions. Do not take them personally.
    4. The comments in this file do nothing. Search engines ignore them. We do not.

  Fun facts about this file:
    The numbers on the site come from balloons that rose about thirty kilometres and then came back down.
    A balloon sensor measures the air about once a second, all the way up.
    We only keep the lowest reading, the one near the ground. That is the one you can feel.
    The data comes from volunteers with antennas on their roofs. They deserve a medal. Several medals.
    The server lives in a home, on Wi-Fi, between a shelf and a window. It is doing its best.

  Last updated: 2026-10-15, give or take a balloon.
-->
